WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
How does water get to the top of a plant?

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.400
A celery stalk and blue water make its path visible.

3
00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.960
You'll compare a stalk with leaves to one without.

4
00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:17.250
Setting up takes about twenty minutes, plus a few short checks over a day.

5
00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.890
Your child makes a guess, waits, and checks it.

6
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:24.310
They practice looking closely at something slow.

7
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.650
And they see a path inside a plant that is normally hidden.

8
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.540
If anyone is allergic to celery, leave it out for everyone.

9
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.160
Use the guide's napa cabbage option instead.

10
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.400
Keep all experiment plants out of mouths.

11
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.860
The setup that follows is for celery.

12
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.420
Choose food coloring everyone can use safely.

13
00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.440
If no coloring is suitable, skip the activity.

14
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:57.970
You need three celery stalks with leaves, three sturdy clear glasses, and blue or

15
00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:58.970
red food coloring.

16
00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.450
Yellow is hard to see.

17
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:07.150
Add water, a tray, paper towels, and old clothes, because the coloring stains.

18
00:01:08.383 --> 00:01:11.623
Fill each glass with about five centimeters of water.

19
00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:15.683
Stir in fifteen to twenty drops of coloring per glass.

20
00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.803
Dark color is much easier to see.

21
00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.087
You do all the cutting.

22
00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:26.487
Keep celery pieces and small dye caps away from children under four.

23
00:01:27.707 --> 00:01:29.327
Call nine one one if choking.

24
00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:34.107
Trim about two centimeters from each base just before setup.

25
00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:36.927
Cut all the leaves off one stalk.

26
00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:40.483
Before they go in, hold up both stalks.

27
00:01:41.903 --> 00:01:43.683
Ask, 'Where do you think the blue will go?'

28
00:01:44.163 --> 00:01:48.323
Then ask, 'Which one will change first, the one with leaves or the one without?'

29
00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:49.983
Write down the guesses.

30
00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:55.413
Stand the leafy stalk and the leafless stalk in two glasses of the same color.

31
00:01:56.713 --> 00:01:58.273
Keep the third stalk as a spare.

32
00:01:59.533 --> 00:02:01.453
Find a bright spot out of direct sun.

33
00:02:02.713 --> 00:02:05.133
Stay nearby while the colored water is out.

34
00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.833
Now a question for you.

35
00:02:09.153 --> 00:02:12.033
Tomorrow you will cut across the leafy stalk, above the water.

36
00:02:13.213 --> 00:02:15.253
What do you think the cut end will look like?

37
00:02:16.293 --> 00:02:17.893
Blue all over, or something else?

38
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:25.197
Check after about one hour.

39
00:02:26.517 --> 00:02:27.517
Little may show yet.

40
00:02:28.657 --> 00:02:33.557
After about four hours, blue lines most often climb the ribs, and the leaf edges

41
00:02:33.557 --> 00:02:36.777
start to color. Compare the two stalks.

42
00:02:38.017 --> 00:02:39.177
Ask, 'Was your guess right?'

43
00:02:40.217 --> 00:02:44.777
The next day usually gives the clearest result, with blue veins in the leaves.

44
00:02:46.137 --> 00:02:49.357
Cut across the stalk about three centimeters above the water.

45
00:02:50.657 --> 00:02:52.357
Look for a curved row of blue dots.

46
00:02:53.677 --> 00:02:56.537
Each dot marks a bundle that contains water tubes.

47
00:02:57.617 --> 00:02:59.377
Here is why the leaves matter.

48
00:03:00.797 --> 00:03:03.117
Water dries off through tiny pores in the leaves.

49
00:03:04.377 --> 00:03:07.797
As it leaves, it pulls more water up the tubes behind it.

50
00:03:08.897 --> 00:03:11.537
So the stalk with leaves usually colors faster.

51
00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:15.410
Stay nearby while the colored water is out.

52
00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:20.590
Use sturdy glasses that won't tip, kept away from toddlers and pets.

53
00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.790
Nobody eats the celery or drinks the colored water.

54
00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.330
Throw both away, and wash hands with soap.

55
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:33.053
To finish, ask, 'Where did the water go in, and where did it go?'

56
00:03:33.633 --> 00:03:35.433
The color only made the path visible.

57
00:03:36.673 --> 00:03:38.313
With clear water, it still climbs.

58
00:03:39.553 --> 00:03:40.693
We just can't see it.
